  "mapping": "MPFB target deltas transfer onto ANY suite character mesh via KD-tree nearest-surface mapping (same as cape-jones mpfb_wire_cj.py): bake as shape keys MPFB_<id>, each driven 0.0..1.0 (or -1..1). 0 = neutral.",
  "source": "MPFB2 v2.0.18 (makehumancommunity/mpfb2) — code GPL-3.0-or-later, data/targets CC0-1.0. Pulled into mhvnsnt/cape-jones production/tools/mpfb2 (PR #128 merged). Target paths below resolve against mpfb2 src/mpfb/data/targets/. Headless recipe: cape-jones production/tools/mpfb2/WIRING.md.",
  "ui": "packages/creation-suite/src/morphs.js exposes BODY_MORPHS for the front end; customization/create-fighter gets a Body tab with these sliders.",
  "anatomy_layers": {
    "source": "docs/research/ANATOMY-LAYERS-SPEC-2026-10-23.md",
    "schema": "wh.anatomy-layers/1",
    "generator": "tools/anatomy/generate_layers.py",
    "layers": [
      "BONE — simplified bone volumes from the skeleton (skull, ribcage, pelvis, limb capsules) as analytic SDF primitives",
      "MUSCLE — muscle-group volumes (pecs, abs, biceps, quads, ...) as analytic SDF primitives attached to bones, 25 groups each with a bulk morph parameter",
      "FAT — offset shell layer: per-region subcutaneous thickness (6 regions + global)",
      "SKIN — the existing render mesh, referenced never copied, + MPFB morph-target hooks"
    ],
    "per_fighter_data": "roster/<fighter>/anatomy/anatomy-layers.json",
    "bake_path": "tools/anatomy/generate_layers.py bake_displacement(): per-vertex displacement along skin normals = (muscle SDF base − morphed) + (fat morphed − base). Anatomy dials compose additively with MPFB shape keys (final = base + sum(dial*delta)); they never replace MPFB dials.",
    "suite_dials": "packages/creation-suite/src/morphs.js exposes ANATOMY_LAYER_MORPHS (37 dials: 25 muscle_bulk + 7 fat + 5 bone_scale) + composeMorphVector() for the morphing UI crew.",
    "note": "v1 layers are procedural from the skeleton + body-part regions measured from the mesh. The morphing UI itself is owned by another crew."
  }
}
